//? Title: Successive halving, Hyperband, ASHA and population-based training
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

> Successive halving, Hyperband and ASHA

Successive halving promotes strong trials to larger fidelities. Hyperband
varies the starting fidelity and cohort size across brackets. ASHA
promotes from completed observations without a synchronized barrier.
A promotion from fidelity r to s consumes s−r additional units and keeps
the same trial. Its score is compared to other trials at fidelity s.

> Population-based training

Population-based training advances checkpoints in synchronous rounds.
Weak workers inherit trained state from donors and explore new
hyperparameters before the next round. Work used to train the donor
checkpoint remains charged to the original trial.

See [Li et al., Hyperband|https://jmlr.org/papers/v18/16-558.html],
[Li et al., ASHA|https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.05934],
and [Jaderberg et al.|https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.09846].

> Stateful toy training

Each checkpoint has a target parameter and an error that decays during
training. The uniform starting draw determines the parameter, and every
checkpoint exposes the actual cumulative resource at each callback.
ASHA durations vary deterministically across workers. Four fixed seeds
are used at each budget. The plotted metric is the selected checkpoint's
observed loss at the highest fidelity reached. The table includes consumed
resource, achieved fidelity and all four seeds at the largest budget.

```{cpp, id=trial-schedulers, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <random>
#include <stdexcept>

struct Worker {
    double parameter;
    double error{1};
    std::size_t reached{};
};

double train(Worker& worker, std::size_t previous, std::size_t target) {
    if (worker.reached != previous) throw std::runtime_error("Lost trial continuity");
    const auto delta = worker.parameter - 0.4;
    worker.error *= std::pow(0.82 + 0.14*std::abs(delta), target - previous);
    worker.reached = target;
    return worker.error + delta*delta;
}

int main() {
    namespace o = dm::optim;
    constexpr std::array<std::uint64_t, 4> seeds{1,7,42,123};
    const std::vector<std::string> labels{"Successive halving","Hyperband","ASHA","PBT"};
    const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGBA> colors{{30,99,168},{205,99,31},{45,138,83},{137,72,155}};
    const std::array methods{o::ResourceSearchMethod::successive_halving, o::ResourceSearchMethod::hyperband,
                             o::ResourceSearchMethod::asha};
    const std::vector<double> budgets{24, 48, 96, 192};
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    std::print("| Method | Seed | Budget | Consumed | Fidelity | Loss |\n"
               "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t method = 0; method < labels.size(); ++method) {
        std::vector<double> mean(budgets.size());
        for (const auto seed : seeds) {
            for (std::size_t i = 0; i < budgets.size(); ++i) {
                const auto budget = static_cast<std::size_t>(budgets[i]);
                std::vector<Worker> checkpoints;
                const auto start = [&](std::size_t id, std::uint64_t seed) {
                    if (id != checkpoints.size()) throw std::runtime_error("Invalid trial ID");
                    std::mt19937_64 rng(seed);
                    checkpoints.push_back({std::uniform_real_distribution<double>()(rng)});
                };
                double loss;
                std::size_t consumed, resource;
                if (method < methods.size()) {
                    o::ResourceSearchOptions options;
                    options.method = methods[method];
                    options.resource_budget = budget;
                    options.seed = seed;
                    options.trials = 16;
                    options.maximum_resource = 16;
                    const auto run = o::resource_search(start,
                        [&](std::size_t id, std::size_t previous, std::size_t target) {
                            return train(checkpoints[id], previous, target);
                        }, options, [](std::size_t id, std::size_t added) { return (1 + id%3)*double(added); });
                    loss = run.best->loss;
                    consumed = run.consumed;
                    resource = run.best->resource;
                } else {
                    std::mt19937_64 rng(seed);
                    for (std::size_t w = 0; w < 6; ++w) start(w, rng());
                    const auto explore = [](Worker& worker, auto& engine) {
                        worker.parameter = std::clamp(worker.parameter + std::normal_distribution<double>(0, 0.1)(engine), 0.0, 1.0);
                    };
                    const auto run = o::population_based_training(std::move(checkpoints), train, explore,
                                                                   {budget, seed, 2, 16, 1});
                    loss = run.best->loss;
                    consumed = run.consumed;
                    resource = run.best->resource;
                }
                if (consumed > budget) throw std::runtime_error("Resource cap exceeded");
                mean[i] += loss / seeds.size();
                if (i + 1 == budgets.size()) {
                    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} |\n", labels[method], seed,
                               budget, consumed, resource, loss);
                }
            }
        }
        plot.line(budgets, mean, labels[method], colors[method]);
    }
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
    plot.title("Best observed checkpoint at highest fidelity").x_label("Total resource budget")
        .y_label("Mean validation loss").legend(labels, colors).size(850,470)
        .save_svg("build/trial_schedulers.svg");
    std::filesystem::copy_file("build/trial_schedulers.svg", "figures/trial_schedulers.svg",
                               std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
```
